Package: mica-wifi-ap
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mica build <mica@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: hostapd, rfkill, iw
Description: Mica OS Wi-Fi access-point support
 Masks hostapd.service by symlinking it to /dev/null, and ships the
 etc-hostapd.mount that binds /etc/hostapd from the STATE partition together
 with its local-fs.target.wants link.
 .
 hostapd@.service is left INSTALLED AND UNENABLED. micad's access-point
 reconciler starts the instance for the interface it brought up and renders
 that instance's configuration file; the distribution's non-templated unit
 would start a second hostapd against a configuration nothing wrote.
 .
 The bind mount is not a convenience. On the Mica OS image /etc is inside the
 read-only dm-verity squashfs, so without it the provisioning access point --
 the path to a device's first configuration -- never comes up, and the AP
 pre-shared key would not survive an A/B update.
 .
 Station support is mica-wifi, a separate package. A board that only serves an
 access point installs this one alone, and a board that only joins networks
 installs neither hostapd nor this package. rfkill is required because the
 radio is soft-blocked out of the box on the boards this image targets.
 .
 The authenticated kernel support image supplies regulatory.db and its
 signature before userspace starts. iw reloads cfg80211's database before
 configuring radio interfaces.
